# ==============================================================================================
# GitHub Pages serves this repository's root directly, so anything committed here is PUBLISHED.
# That makes an accidental node_modules/ commit worse than untidy — it would be served.
#
# BENCH.md's setup step is `npm i three`, run from the repo root because that is where
# render.mjs and preview.mjs live. That drops three build artefacts into the root every time.
# None of them belong in the repo: the bench is a dev tool, and the scene itself takes three.js
# from the importmap in world-nav.html, not from node_modules.
# ==============================================================================================
node_modules/

# Created by `npm i three`. The repo deliberately has no manifest — if one is ever added on
# purpose, `git add -f package.json` overrides this line.
package.json
package-lock.json

# preview.mjs writes <name>-plan.png, <name>-oblique.png and <name>-horizon.png beside itself.
# Bench output is meant to be looked at and thrown away; the committed imagery is .webp.
*-plan.png
*-oblique.png
*-horizon.png
